416 0 obj
<<
/ActualText (This is an interactive sound installation composed of three suspended handles. Drawing on the familiar image of handrails in public transportation, the work temporarily creates a shared space for multiple participants without requiring cooperation. Each participant alters their own independent sound by grasping and pulling the handles\024where the force, rhythm, and duration of movement affect the sound's state. When participants' actions briefly synchronize, the system may produce a unified acoustic transformation. The piece explores how multiple independent individuals coexist within a shared environment, perceive one another, and occasionally form fleeting connections.)
/K [3]
/S /Span
/Type /StructElem
/P 417 0 R
/Pg 199 0 R
>>
