951 0 obj
<<
/ActualText (This project originated from my personal experience riding a mountain bus. As the crowded vehicle navigated sharp turns, passengers shifted their center of gravity, grabbed handrails, and constantly adjusted their postures to adapt to the motion of the bus\024being influenced by the road conditions. I am interested in these subtle bodily responses during travel, as they transform the ordinary act of moving into an embodied experience. In my initial proposal, I temporarily described the body as "an expression of motion itself," understanding the passenger's body as a medium through which environmental forces become perceptible.)
/K [3]
/S /Span
/Type /StructElem
/P 952 0 R
/Pg 420 0 R
>>
endobj
952 0 obj
<<
/K [951 0 R]
/S /P
/Type /StructElem
/P 945 0 R
>>
endobj
