957 0 obj
<<
/ActualText (An important early theoretical reference was Tim Ingold\031s Lines: A Brief History. Ingold regards 'wandering' as a vibrant, responsive movement, contrasting it with point-to-point transportation logic\( Ingold, 2007, pp.73-77, pp.101\). This gave me a way of thinking about what is lost when a journey is reduced to origin and destination. My initial question was whether the apparently flattened \034in-between\035 of transport could be reopened through bodily sensation: could the small tensions, movements and vibrations that remain in the body reveal another form of experience inside this connecting line? This question formed the conceptual basis of the first proposal.\n)
/K [6]
/S /Span
/Type /StructElem
/P 958 0 R
/Pg 420 0 R
>>
endobj
958 0 obj
