962 0 obj
<<
/K [961 0 R]
/S /P
/Type /StructElem
/P 945 0 R
>>
endobj
963 0 obj
<<
/ActualText (However, the project gradually abandoned a literal reconstruction of the "bus journey." Public transportation, rather than being the subject of my project, functions more as a spatial and social reference within it. The suspended handrail is a familiar object associated with a shared environment in which strangers temporarily occupy the same structure.\nFor this reason, I use the transport handle as a shorthand for a public condition: it allows me to establish a temporary shared space quickly without constructing an entire transport environment. The work therefore does not attempt to simulate a bus, reproduce a specific route or tell a narrative about transportation. Instead, the visual language of public transport provides a framework in which several people can enter, act independently and remain aware of one another.)
/K [9]
/S /Span
/Type /StructElem
/P 964 0 R
/Pg 420 0 R
>>
endobj
