/ActualText (This shift also changed my understanding of \030participation\031. During the bus journey I initially mentioned, I observed that strangers sometimes let out nearly identical exclamations when the bus made a sharp turn, even though they spoke different languages. At first, I described this phenomenon as a brief resonance among strangers.My first proposal translated this observation into a much more explicit system: several participants would be subjected to a shared virtual force, and simultaneous tension peaks would briefly merge their individual sounds into a collective voice.)
/K [1]
/S /Span
/Type /StructElem
/P 1377 0 R
/Pg 967 0 R
>>
