/ActualText (As the project developed,however, I became less interested in reproducing synchronisation as a designed outcome. If synchronisation became something participants were expected to discover or achieve, the installation risked becoming a collaborative game with an implicit success condition. I instead wanted the work to remain valid when one person interacted alone, when two people ignored one another, or when three people acted independently. A relationship between participants could emerge, but it should not be required for the system to function.)
/K [4]
/S /Span
/Type /StructElem
/P 1383 0 R
/Pg 967 0 R
>>
endobj
1383 0 obj
<<
