2226 0 obj
<<
/ActualText (At the same time, I had long planned to map stretch into data as an input, and Martinez Avila provided a precedent for this. His project The Stretchy Strap developed an elastic guitar strap that uses body and postural movements as inputs for interacting with digital media. Researchers constructed textile strain sensors using elastic fabric and conductive yarn; changes in resistance were read through a voltage divider circuit and sampled by a Bela embedded computer. At this point, I became familiar with the Bela board and began using it, and the initial outline of this project started to take shape.\nIn summary, this project integrates physical computing, interactive sound, and participatory space. Its evolution has shifted from an early interest in passively engaging with the environment through the body, toward a relational system in which body, object, sensing technology, and sound continuously influence one another, co-shaping each other's experiences.)
