/ActualText (This device uses familiar public object handles to suggest participant actions, eliminating the need to learn complex abstract interfaces. The interactive system employs simple physical interactions, as shown in the left image: participants grasp, pull, hold, and release any of the suspended handrails. When a handle is pulled, the tension in the sensing material changes, resulting in a corresponding change in resistance. The Bela board reads these analog values and converts them in real time via PureData into sound output through DIY speakers. Thus, the most critical component is the stretch sensor section, illustrated in the right image.)
/K [6]
/S /Span
/Type /StructElem
/P 2836 0 R
/Pg 2230 0 R
>>
endobj
