/ActualText (Once the three-hand system was assembled, I conducted wall-mounting tests. The results revealed another series of critical practical issues. During testing, one sensor broke under load, indicating that the sensing material and cable pathways remained too fragile for repeated use. To address this, I added additional mechanical protections: limiters were installed to prevent overextension, and heat-shrink tubing was inserted into drilled holes in the wooden structure to reduce wear at points where sensors passed through the wood.)
