/ActualText (The project significantly expanded my technical practice. My early research into e-textiles led me to experiment with constructing my own pressure and stretch sensors. Although these prototypes remained unstable, I gained a practical understanding of conductive materials, resistance-based sensing and the difficulties of designing deformable interfaces.\nWorking with Bela and Pure Data was another major development. My previous experience with Arduino and Max/MSP made the underlying logic familiar, allowing me to adapt relatively quickly, but this was my first time building a standalone real-time sensing and sound system with these tools. The project has left me particularly interested in the intersection between soft or textile interfaces and sound, which I would like to continue exploring beyond this project.)
/K [8]
/S /Span
