4205 0 obj
<<
/ActualText (Working with Bela and Pure Data was another major development. My previous experience with Arduino and Max/MSP made the underlying logic familiar, allowing me to adapt relatively quickly, but this was my first time building a standalone real-time sensing and sound system with these tools. The project has left me particularly interested in the intersection between soft or textile interfaces and sound, which I would like to continue exploring beyond this project.\nI also learned considerably more about physical installation. My initial plans underestimated the amount of time required for mounting, load testing, cable management and mechanical protection. Because several of the technologies were new to me, I should have reserved substantially more time for full-scale installation testing rather than treating it as the final stage after the electronics were working.\nAt the same time, the project made me recognise the value of communicating problems early. Regular updates to technicians, tutors and my supervisor often produced straightforward solutions to problems that had felt difficult when working alone. I also began keeping a development journal more consistently. Recording what had been achieved, what was still unresolved and what needed to happen the following day became an unexpectedly useful working method. The journal contains not only progress notes but sensor ranges, threshold decisions and installation problems\024for example, recording different resting and active ranges for individual sensors rather than relying on memory.  This reduced the cognitive load of returning to the project each day and made the development process easier to evaluate retrospectively.)
/K [1]
/S /Span
/Type /StructElem
/P 4206 0 R
/Pg 3940 0 R
>>
endobj
